WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.500
By the time of the late 1990s, the days of
the traveling salesman were on the gradual

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.500
decline.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.300
More and more consumers out there were being
all too easily enticed by the alluring draw

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.429
of advertisements broadcast directly into
their homes through their television sets,

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:18.710
or beamed out over the radio between the latest
chart hits.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.560
Hell, even catalogs sent straight to people’s
mailboxes were making it all the harder for

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.860
the door to door industry to stay afloat.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.789
Times, they were a-changing, and everyday
working people were no longer content to allow

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:37.280
a total stranger to stand on their front porch
and peddle their wares at them.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.320
Jerry had been at that game for almost twenty
years now.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.610
He had been born with a natural gift of the
gab that made him a real savant of sales,

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.920
a Michelangelo of making people part with
their hard-earned money, a Da Vinci of discounts

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.750
and dealing, if you will.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.330
Okay, I’ll stop now.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.330
Sorry.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:59.160
His fellow salesmen on the road sometimes
called him ‘Mr Motor Mouth’ - Not to be

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.050
confused with SCP-2094.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.350
They used to joke that Jerry could talk his
way out of a sealed room with no doors or

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.009
windows, while also convincing said room pay
him an exit fee as well.

00:01:11.009 --> 00:01:16.450
But, as much as he had a knack for making
deals, he had felt the tides shifting lately.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.130
The business of driving across the country
to sell products direct to customers was fast

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:26.579
becoming a thing of the past, an almost arcane
practise in the age of the infomercial and

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:29.759
the catchy jingles of advertisements.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:34.100
Companies were growing, becoming far bigger,
absorbing one another to the point where they

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:39.200
were conglomerates, corporations that could
form entire departments dedicated to marketing

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.279
campaigns for their various products.

00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:47.380
They no longer needed the work of men on the
ground, talking face to face with consumers.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.479
Even the smaller companies were giving up
on that method of marketing, choosing instead

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:56.929
to sell their patents and products to the
big boys in exchange for a hefty sum.

00:01:56.929 --> 00:02:02.009
His job as a door to door salesman was on
its way to an inevitable grave, and Jerry

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:03.009
knew it.

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:07.270
With the looming threat of occupational redundancy
on the horizon, he had decided that it was

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.680
time to cash out, to give up a life on the
road and either find a new job somewhere,

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.790
or face the prospect of going flat broke.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.120
But it was hard to leave the scene if you
didn’t have the green.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.290
Between the expenses of keeping his car in
tip top shape to take him from state to state,

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.269
and the ever increasing cut his marketing
agency took out of his earnings, Jerry needed

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:31.489
to see out just one more quarter.

00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:37.260
It wouldn’t be too hard, he thought to himself,
not for old Mr Jerry Motor Mouth.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:43.890
Little did he know, the sales game had a new
player on the board, one whose powers of persuasion

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.970
were far greater than Jerry ever could have
imagined…

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:52.629
A small company that sold its own brand of
food processors had employed the sales agency

00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:53.790
that he worked for.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:58.159
And, seeing as Jerry was one of the few old
guard, classic door to door salesmen that

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:04.049
hadn’t been laid off or let go – yet – he
was off on the open road for what he hoped

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.700
would be the final time.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.010
His windows down, the sweet, timely sounds
of R.E.M.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.299
blasting on his radio, Jerry drove into the
next town on his list.

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:18.049
The last ten places he had stopped in had
all been a nightmare for shifting units, meaning

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:21.480
he still had boxes upon boxes of stock to
shift.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.560
Currently, said cardboard boxes were cramping
up the backseats of his car, with more threatening

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.260
to burst from the trunk and the towbar cargo
box affixed to the rear bumper of his old

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.770
Plymouth Utility.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:37.730
But it seemed like no matter what city, town
or suburb he arrived at, with his car full

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:43.379
of food processors to sell, Jerry kept finding
that he had arrived only too late.

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:46.760
“Oh, no thanks,” the homeowners he visited
would say.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.439
“I just bought a new food processor, the
ad on TV just really sold it to me.”

00:03:52.439 --> 00:03:57.129
Everywhere he turned, every door that he rapped
his knuckles on, all brought the same answer

00:03:57.129 --> 00:03:58.139
with it.

00:03:58.139 --> 00:04:03.379
Naturally, eleven locations in and barely
more than a few units sold, Jerry was starting

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:06.920
to worry his magic motor mouth had run out
of steam.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.879
Had he really lost his knack?

00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:13.939
Or was this rival food processor manufacturer
simply pilfering all his potential customers

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:15.849
through their ad campaign?

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:20.359
After another unsuccessful day, those were
the only questions spinning around and around

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:25.180
in Jerry’s head as he paced back and forth
in the motel room he was staying in.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:30.870
The TV was on, playing an ad break between
a rerun of an episode of Seinfeld, just proving

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.580
some light background noise…

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.160
although it would soon present the answer
to Jerry’s questions.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.810
The chime of a catchy, cheesy jingle caught
his attention first, followed by the name

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:41.810
of the company.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:47.129
It was the same name Jerry had heard from
the lips of every home he’d stopped at.

00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:51.550
This was the commercial that convinced them
all to buy this company’s food processor

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.400
over the ones he was trying to sell.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.430
Grabbing the remote, Jerry jabbed the button
that increased the volume; he had to see how

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.500
they did it.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.800
A large man, considerably overweight by some
people’s standards, appeared on screen and

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:10.340
started rattling off all sorts of details
about the rival company’s food processor.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:16.180
At first, Jerry couldn’t help glaring at
the man, like they were bitter, lifelong enemies.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:20.389
After all, it was because of this ad that
he was missing out on potential sales, and

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:22.979
risking not meeting his final quarterly quota.

00:05:22.979 --> 00:05:27.530
But the more he watched the weighty man on
the screen, telling the viewer how wonderful

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:33.610
this product was, it was like Jerry could
feel a tiny part of himself agreeing.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:39.930
Every word made sense somehow, like it was
just right, unequivocally, unquestionably,

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.990
categorically correct in every way.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.810
He couldn’t refute that this other food
processor, despite being sold by his client’s

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.050
competition, did seem like the superior product.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:56.330
“And if any of you folks need to be persuaded
further, then believe me when I tell you this,”

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.370
the man declared with a wide smile on his
red, sweat sheened face.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.550
“You need this product in your life.”

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.699
He couldn’t argue with that, Jerry thought
to himself; he really did need one of those

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:09.810
food processors.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:14.729
It wasn’t an all consuming, uncontrollable
need – at least, not yet – but more of

00:06:14.729 --> 00:06:19.700
a gentle compulsion that became logged at
the back of his mind.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:23.949
Something about the man’s words had him
pretty convinced, and he had to recognize

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:29.159
and even respect a fellow Salvador Dali of
the salesman’s craft.

00:06:29.159 --> 00:06:33.449
His demeanour wasn’t exactly what you might
expect to see from someone presenting an ad,

00:06:33.449 --> 00:06:37.210
there was no cheesy, jovial banter and forced,
false laughter.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:42.409
In fact, the man had been pretty abrasive,
practically demanding the viewer to buy that

00:06:42.409 --> 00:06:44.879
particular brand of food processor.

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:51.919
And yet, somehow, it seemed to leave a lasting
– albeit fleeting – impression on Jerry…

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:54.909
an impression that would only get worse the
next day.

00:06:54.909 --> 00:06:59.530
He had decided to change his sales tactic,
drawing on an old trick from his two decades

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.040
of experience.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:06.259
After barely selling any of his stock to homeowners,
Jerry figured his next best move was to try

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:11.099
his luck at local restaurants, cafes, and
any other type of business that might have

00:07:11.099 --> 00:07:13.780
need of a new food processor.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:19.600
Maybe, he thought to himself, if he was extremely
lucky, he could sell multiple units of stock

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:25.040
to each business he visited, making up for
the lack of sales he’d made so far.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.069
But it was while driving through the center
of town that something caught Jerry’s eye.

00:07:29.069 --> 00:07:34.120
It was magnetic, like a moth being drawn to
the bright glare of a lightbulb.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:39.130
It was one of the food processors from the
advert, the same ones that everyone Jerry

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.560
had visited had already bought.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:48.030
There it sat in a storefront window, as if
it was practically beckoning him inside.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:53.340
The man on TV had told Jerry he needed one
for himself, and now that he could see it

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:56.729
as clear as day, he knew that was true.

00:07:56.729 --> 00:08:01.539
For the next few minutes, it was like Jerry’s
brain had been set to autopilot mode.

00:08:01.539 --> 00:08:06.199
He parked his car, turned the engine off,
opened the door and started walking towards

00:08:06.199 --> 00:08:09.550
the store without stopping to think about
it at all.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:15.990
Within minutes, he was not only inside, but
lifting a heavy box off the shelf and carrying

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:21.060
the shiny new food processor – the ones
sold by a company that were rivals to his

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.490
very own clients – up to the cashier.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:29.629
Still not pausing to even consider what he
was doing, as if he had been put in a trance,

00:08:29.629 --> 00:08:35.700
Jerry opened up his wallet and parted with
his hard earned cash, paying for the processor

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.290
and carrying it back to his car.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:42.420
It wasn’t until he sat back down in the
driver’s seat, that Jerry seemed to wake

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:47.010
up, only to look in horror at the box he had
just placed in the seat next to him.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:51.010
He blinked, his face awash with disbelief.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:56.190
Never in all his years had he ever needed
something like a food processor, he had no

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.190
use for it.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:02.280
But now he had just gone and absentmindedly
purchased one, from a rival brand no less…

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:07.880
and it had all been because that man on the
TV had told him he needed to.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.300
He couldn’t go back to making sales that
day, how could he?

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.680
Even if he could get any of the town’s local
restaurants interested in buying the food

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.920
processors he had to sell, they would immediately
lose all faith in the product the minute they

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:25.320
spotted a different brand of the same device
sitting pristine in Jerry’s car.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:30.340
Driving back to the motel, he just spent a
few hours sitting on the uncomfortable bed,

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.250
staring blankly in awe at what he had bought.

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:38.120
Overcome with a sudden rush of anger, although
mainly directed at himself, he hurled the

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.080
box across the room.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.660
It banged loudly against the wall, then clattered
to the floor.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.790
But it was just as he marched over to it,
about to stomp on the food processor with

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:51.311
his foot, that Jerry spotted something printed
on the back.

00:09:51.311 --> 00:09:56.320
It was hidden among all the usual legal speak
that companies were required to have on their

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.960
products: ‘Not satisfied with this product?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.400
Call our Customer Service hotline!’.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:06.910
It was those few simple words, and the string
of numbers that followed it, that gave Jerry

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:07.910
an idea.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:13.820
That man on the TV, someone at the rival company
must have hired him to present the advertisement.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:19.170
And if he could find out who, and get in touch
with that oddly convincing man, that could

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.870
be the answer to his sales trouble…

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:27.830
little did Jerry expect that it would lead
to a whole different type of trouble for him.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:32.690
It definitely didn’t come easy, starting
with a call to the company’s customer complaints

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.310
departments with the hope of being put through
to their advertising people was an uphill

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.660
challenge for anyone.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:44.560
But Jerry wasn’t just anyone, he was Mr
Motor Mouth, the man who could talk his way

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.240
into and out of anything.

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:53.000
He knew he’d have to lie through his teeth,
or ‘bend the truth’ as he liked to call

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.000
it.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.080
Each time he claimed to be from the Federal
Trade Commission or the United States Patent

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:02.850
and Trademark office, a cold tremble shuddered
through his hands, heart pounding faster against

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:07.250
his chest, icy sweat making his shirt stick
to his back.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:11.900
Every lie was a risk, he could easily be reported
to the police for fraud.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:17.450
But, by some miracle – or maybe a curse
– his phone call was passed from department

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:22.790
to department until he spoke to one of the
companies advertising personnel.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:26.980
They were careless enough to give him the
address of the man who had been in their TV

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:30.930
ads... and it was only a short drive across
town.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:34.550
Unlike earlier, Jerry was now fully aware
of what he was doing.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:38.940
He just couldn’t believe he was actually
going through with it.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:43.100
Standing outside the front door of the man
from the advertisement, the one who had seemingly

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:48.450
mesmerized him into buying something he didn’t
even need, he could feel his pulse beating

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.450
faster than ever.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.130
Reaching out a shaking hand, he knocked loudly
on the door.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:59.410
The sound of movement came from behind the
door, only for it to be pulled open.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:03.230
There he was, standing in the doorframe.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:07.200
Although he’d never say it out loud, Jerry
couldn’t help but wonder how such a large

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.880
man fit through his own doorway.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:15.140
He somehow looked worse up close; the cameras
and makeup for the ad must have gone a long

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:20.910
way to mask just how very clear it was that
this man wasn’t exactly the model of perfect

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:21.910
health.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.080
“Can I help you?” he asked abruptly.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.190
“Y-yes, sorry,” Jerry stammered nervously.

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.990
“My name’s Jerry.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:33.510
I saw you on a TV ad last night… for a food
processor.”

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.600
“I’m not giving out autographs.”

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.460
The man wasn’t just blunt, he was outright
impolite.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.320
“Beat it, Jerry.”

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:44.110
“Wait!” he interjected, desperation making
his voice crack.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.470
“Please, just let me explain.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:50.040
I work in sales and I’ve got a car full
of similar products that I need to get people

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.040
to buy.”

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:53.060
“And you want me to help with that?”

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.110
the man predicted.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:55.110
“Not interested.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:57.760
I only do ads if I’m getting paid.”

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:02.110
By now, the sheer overwhelming nerves that
had taken hold of Jerry were quickly becoming

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.590
something else.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:08.540
Hearing how bad-mannered and unaccommodating
this man was being made it hard to keep his

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:09.800
temper.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:15.310
Frustration was boiling over into anger, and
eventually, it became too much to keep down

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.980
any longer.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:22.640
Jerry reached too hands out to the man, gripping
his thick neck by the folds of his sweat-soaked

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:23.640
collar.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:28.650
“Listen to me, you!” he said, his voice
raised as his rage came bursting out.

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:32.360
“I haven’t been able to sell one of these
damn things, and it’s all because of that

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.080
stupid ad you were in!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:38.060
You even got me to buy one, I still have no
idea how!

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:42.981
I’m a door-to-door salesman for crying out
loud, what on earth would I ever want with

00:13:42.981 --> 00:13:44.490
a food processor?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.190
Tell me how you did it!”

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:49.150
“You want to take your hands off me, Jerry.”

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:53.610
The man’s voice was calm, almost unnerving
in how reserved he was being.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:58.460
Before he had addressed Jerry dismissively,
but now he spoke with a collected, simplicity.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.600
And it worked.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.380
Somehow, it worked.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:07.200
As if his arms were moving independently,
Jerry watched as his hands let go of the man’s

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.820
collar, staring wide-eyed.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:13.430
He hadn’t wanted to take them away, hadn’t
made an effort to let go.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:19.690
Except, the moment he was told that he wanted
to, he had wanted to, and loosened his grip

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.130
accordingly.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:25.430
The man had told him what he wanted and somehow
made it true.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.250
“Who… what are you?”

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.910
Jerry asked, looking up in horror at the larger
man.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:38.190
“You want to not harm me,” the man replied
with that same, eerie calmness to his voice.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:43.070
But there was something else there too, a
low tone of another, far crueler cadence.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:47.390
“You want to hurt yourself though, Jerry.”

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:51.090
Something came speeding through the air and
caught the side of Jerry’s cheek.

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:55.610
The force of the object reeled him, causing
him to stagger back until he realized exactly

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.950
what had hit him: it was his own fist.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:02.610
He’d punched himself… no, it was worse
than that.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:08.050
He had wanted to harm himself, just like the
man had told him.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:13.980
“I think what you really want,” the other
man continued, using a tone that now swam

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.820
with even more sadistic malice.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:19.070
“Is to keep hitting yourself.”

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:24.500
The pain of another self-inflicted punch struck
Jerry, followed swiftly by a third.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:29.560
His arms were moving impulsively, almost like
he had no control over them, but also as if

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:33.740
he couldn’t help but keep doing what this
man had said.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:38.290
His fist clenched tight, an uppercut connected
with Jerry’s chin, causing one of his teeth

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.660
to chip against the other.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:45.040
Spluttering, he spat out the fragment of enamel,
followed by a mouthful of blood and spittle.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.400
“Let me make you an offer that you can’t
refuse,” the man announced.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:55.970
“For the low, low price of nothing at all,
keep punching yourself in the face, as hard

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:56.970
as you can.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.190
It’s the new best thing for you, right Jerry?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:04.530
Don’t stop until you lose consciousness.”

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:10.050
Instantly, Jerry’s fists started pummelling,
striking one after the other.

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:14.390
The pain was pulsating through the skin of
his face, stinging under his eyes, reddening

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:17.170
and bruising every visible part.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:22.740
Another hit connected sharply, and Jerry felt
the agony of his own nose breaking, the crunch

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:27.770
of bone as more blood spilled out of his nostrils,
wetting his mouth and staining it red.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:28.770
The metallic tang of blood washed through
the back of his mouth as he knocked another

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:29.770
of his own teeth loose and accidentally swallowed
it, coughing and spraying more crimson bodily

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.770
fluid over his white work shirt.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:31.770
It went on for hours.

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:35.840
By the time he had hit himself enough times,
Jerry’s face was completely unrecognizable.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:43.340
His face was swollen, jaw dislocated, and
one eye so badly bruised that it had swollen,

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.120
practically shutting itself.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:50.960
His arm raised once more of its own accord
and came slamming down, hard enough to knock

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:54.950
Jerry out, laying in a bloodied and bruised
mess.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:01.630
Looking down at him, SCP-661 sneered, and
went back into his house, slamming the door

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:02.940
behind him.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:06.659
Jerry wasn’t the only one whose attention
had been caught by the advertisements starring

00:17:06.659 --> 00:17:08.539
this particularly rude man.

00:17:08.539 --> 00:17:14.049
They had also garnered the scrutiny of the
SCP Foundation, who had placed this individual

00:17:14.049 --> 00:17:19.639
– later known by the designation SCP-661
– under surveillance.

00:17:19.639 --> 00:17:24.449
For a while, they had kept a close eye on
him, monitoring his day-to-day activity.

00:17:24.449 --> 00:17:29.500
To the untrained eye, he was just an ordinary
– if a little overweight – man working

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.730
as an advertising and marketing agent.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:37.200
He’d regularly star in TV and radio ads,
boasting the wild assertion that he could

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.149
easily convince anyone alive to do anything
he told them.

00:17:41.149 --> 00:17:45.669
Now, sure, arrogance is hardly a purely anomalous
trait.

00:17:45.669 --> 00:17:50.330
But what the Foundation soon realized was,
that claim was right.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:55.910
Testing quickly revealed that SCP-661’s
voice possessed some kind of hypnotic or mesmeric

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.440
influence.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:02.830
Simply by speaking, he could manipulate other
people into doing what he asked them to do,

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.570
or wanting what he told them they wanted.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:10.720
Naturally, working in marketing, this made
him a salesman almost too good to be true,

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:15.899
just as long as someone could understand the
commands and suggestions he made.

00:18:15.899 --> 00:18:19.279
Anyone exposed to his voice would feel a prolonged
sense of compulsion.

00:18:19.279 --> 00:18:24.490
It began as a weak feeling at first, just
lingering in the back of a person’s mind

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:30.429
like a post-hypnotic suggestion; a thought
implanted by somebody else, that the subject

00:18:30.429 --> 00:18:32.710
doesn’t act on until later.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.730
The effect would normally last for around
a week, or until a time when the subject was

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:43.350
presented with the means to actually get what
SCP-661 had convinced them they wanted; say,

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.570
for example, a physical product like a food
processor.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:53.090
Perhaps the worst part though, is that SCP-661
seems to have been aware of his anomalous

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.909
powers of influence for some time.

00:18:55.909 --> 00:19:00.769
Although he claims otherwise, he’s shown
no problem in trying to use his manipulative

00:19:00.769 --> 00:19:06.389
‘gift of the gab’ to convince the Foundation’s
personnel to release him from their custody,

00:19:06.389 --> 00:19:08.460
where he is currently being held.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:12.710
Lucky they bought themselves noise-canceling
headphones; those might be the only things

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:16.570
stopping this slimy salesman from getting
into their heads.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:23.519
Now go and check out “SCP-738 THE DEVIL’S
DEAL” and “SCP-035 THE POSSESSIVE MASK”

00:19:23.519 --> 00:19:28.759
for more anomalies with enticing offers for
unsuspecting humans, that can promise to fulfill

00:19:28.759 --> 00:19:31.460
your deepest desires for a price…

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:34.250
except that price might not be worth paying!

